---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

import talent1 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent1.png';
import talent2 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent2.png';
import talent3 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent3.png';
import talent4 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent4.png';
import talent5 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent5.png';
import talent6 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent6.png';
import talent7 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent7.png';
import talent8 from '../../assets/images/projects/talent/talent8.png';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Talent - Artem Androsov"
  description="Talent — a multi-format content licensing platform for independent creators. 45 screens, interactive Figma prototype, original text licensing category."
  ogImage="/og/talent.jpg"
  activePage="projects"
>
        <div class="back-nav">
            <a href="/" class="back-link">Back to projects</a>
        </div>

        <section class="project-hero" id="hero">
            <div class="section-label">Case study</div>
            <h1>Talent</h1>
            <p class="project-brief">A multi-format content licensing platform for independent creators — one place
                for footage, music, sound effects, images, and licensed scripts. Built from scratch as a concept I'd
                been sitting on for two years and couldn't find anywhere on the market.</p>

            <div class="project-meta">
                <div class="meta-item">
                    <span class="meta-label">My role</span>
                    <span class="meta-value">Product, UX/UI</span>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-item">
                    <span class="meta-label">Areas</span>
                    <div class="meta-tags">
                        <span class="meta-tag">Product Strategy</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">UX/UI</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">Figma</span>
                        <span class="meta-tag">Self-initiated</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-concept" id="concept">
            <div class="www-grid">
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">Why</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">I spent years working with YouTubers and production teams across multiple
                        projects. Everyone ran the same fragmented workflow: Artlist for music, Freepik for images,
                        Envato for footage, a separate tool for sound effects — four subscriptions, four interfaces,
                        four licensing agreements per project. I looked for a platform that consolidated all of this
                        under one roof. It didn't exist. Artlist covers music. Freepik covers images. Nobody unified
                        all four — and nobody had touched licensed text (scripts, voiceover copy) as a category at
                        all. That last gap I hadn't seen anywhere. The problem became impossible to ignore when the
                        entire creator community I worked in lost access to its standard toolstack overnight. A
                        workaround isn't a product. I decided to design the product.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">What</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">I designed Talent from the ground up: a multi-format licensing marketplace
                        covering video footage, music, sound effects, images, and written content (scripts, voiceover
                        copy) under one roof. The UX centrepiece is Mix search — a cross-category query that returns
                        contextually matched results across all content types simultaneously. Search "forest atmosphere"
                        in Mix and get aerial footage, ambient music, bird sounds, wind effects — as a coherent set,
                        not four separate searches. The business model combines two mechanics studied from competitors:
                        Envato's purchase logic (exclusive buy-out removes the work from the platform, signalling
                        scarcity) and Artlist's subscription simplicity (per-category or all-access tiers). The text
                        category — scripts and voiceover copy as licensable assets — I added myself. I hadn't seen it
                        done anywhere. Result: 45 screens, 17 modal states and interactive flows, fully prototyped in
                        Figma with realistic content throughout.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="www-column">
                    <h2 class="www-title">How</h2>
                    <p class="www-text">Competitive analysis before any design: Envato's monetisation architecture,
                        Artlist's tagging and discovery UX, Freepik's multi-format navigation. Each contributed one
                        pattern I took, studied, and improved on. The core IA challenge was unifying fundamentally
                        different content types — video (vertical vs. horizontal), audio (music vs. SFX), images, and
                        text — under a navigation model that felt consistent, not cobbled together. Mix mode required
                        its own logic: a contextual query needed to understand that "nature atmosphere" maps to footage
                        + ambient music + environmental SFX simultaneously. I designed the tag system to support
                        cross-type queries from the ground up. The concept attracted investor interest before the
                        design was complete — the project didn't move forward due to the investor's change of
                        priorities, not product-market fit. A senior web designer who reviewed the prototype called it
                        the strongest case study he'd seen — and he hadn't built anything at that scale of complexity
                        himself.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-gallery" id="gallery">
            <div class="section-label">Process &amp; outcome</div>
            <h2>What it looks like</h2>

            <div class="gallery-grid">
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent1} alt="Talent — image 1" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent2} alt="Talent — image 2" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent3} alt="Talent — image 3" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent4} alt="Talent — image 4" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent5} alt="Talent — image 5" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent6} alt="Talent — image 6" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent7} alt="Talent — image 7" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
                <div class="gallery-item">
                    <Image src={talent8} alt="Talent — image 8" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-results" id="results">
            <div class="section-label">Results</div>
            <h2>What we delivered</h2>

            <div class="metrics-grid">
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">45</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Screens</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Desktop — full subscription flow, purchase flow, creator upload, and Mix discovery mode</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">17</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">States &amp; modals</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Error states, loading flows, modal windows — every interactive layer prototyped</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">5</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Content types</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Video · Audio · Images · SFX · Text — unified under one IA and one licensing model</p>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-card">
                    <span class="metric-number">1</span>
                    <span class="metric-label">Original category</span>
                    <p class="metric-description">Licensed scripts and voiceover copy — a content type not present in any major competitor</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="project-shipped" id="shipped">
            <div class="section-label">What shipped</div>
            <p class="shipped-text">A fully interactive Figma prototype — desktop-first, designed for the professional
                creator workflow. The prototype covers the complete user journey: discovery via search and Mix mode,
                subscription and single-purchase flows, creator upload and profile experience. No mobile version — a
                deliberate scope decision. Two years after the original idea, no direct competitor has launched in
                this space. The market gap is still open.</p>
            <a href="https://www.figma.com/proto/gStDRj2VJso77ljBK1r7U5/Talant?node-id=671-12594&p=f&viewport=685%2C355%2C0.04&t=E8RBR5hKNfLVn6X4-8&scaling=min-zoom&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=385%3A908&page-id=0%3A1&hide-ui=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display: inline-block; margin-top: 12px; color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 500;">View interactive prototype →</a>
        </section>

        <section class="next-project" id="next">
            <div class="section-label">Next project</div>
            <a href="/projects/ourwall" class="next-project-link">
                <span class="next-project-name">Our Wall</span>
                <span class="next-project-arrow">→</span>
            </a>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-section" id="cta">
            <h2>Starting from zero?</h2>
            <p class="contact-subtitle contact-subtitle-margin">
                A blank page is where I do my best work. Tell me about the product.
            </p>
            <a href="https://t.me/androsovart" target="_blank" class="btn-primary" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get in
                touch</a>
        </section>

        <Footer />
</ProjectLayout>
